SI No,Test Case Name,Test Description,Test Objective,Test Category,Test Steps,Expected Results,Register Name,Register Offset (Hex),Register Block,Block Base Offset (Hex),Absolute Register Address (Hex),Fields Accessed,Bit Range,Field Width (bits),Access Type,Reset Value,Read/Write Operation,Values Written,IP_NAME,Source File,Macro Name in Code,Notes
1,pcie_device_enumerate_test,PCIe Device Enumeration Test - Performs link training for PCIe DM0/DM1 in RC/EP modes followed by cache coherency programming and device enumeration including Vendor ID read and BAR memory base programming,Verify PCIe device enumeration flow including link training and cache coherency control and BAR register programming and Vendor ID reading,Functional,"Step 1: Initialize by writing 0x0 to address 0xE6004100.
Step 2: Perform link training for DM0/DM1 in RC/EP mode using link_training_dm0_x4(4) or link_training_dm1_x4(4).
Step 3: Program COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register for PCIE0 - set bits [14:11] to 0xF and bits [6:3] to 0xF (CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_MODE and CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_MODE).
Step 4: Program COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF register for PCIE0 - set bits [30:27] to 0xF and bits [22:19] to 0xF (CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_VALUE and CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_VALUE).
Step 5: Repeat Steps 3-4 for PCIE1 COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF.
Step 6: Wait 20 cycles then re-program PCIE0 and PCIE1 COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF with all cache fields set to 0xF.
Step 7: Poll SII0 register 0xC0 until (data & 0xD1) == 0xD1 indicating link up.
Step 8: Poll SII1 register 0xC0 until (data & 0xD1) == 0xD1 indicating link up.
Step 9: Read Vendor ID from PCIe slave0 register offset 0x0.
Step 10: Write 0x7 to PCIe slave0 command register offset 0x4 to enable IO/Memory/BusMaster.
Step 11: Program memory base for DM0 x4 and DM1 x4.
Step 12: Disable cache programming - set ARCACHE_VALUE and AWCACHE_VALUE to 0x0 in COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF for both PCIE0 and PCIE1.
Step 13: Write 0xFFFFFFFF to PCIe slave BAR registers (offsets 0x10-0x24) to determine BAR size.
Step 14: Read back BAR registers to get size information.
Step 15: Program BAR registers with actual base addresses.
Step 16: Read back programmed BAR values to verify.
Step 17: Poll address 0xE6004100 until value equals 0x12345678 indicating test completion.","Link training completes successfully for configured mode.
SII link status shows 0xD1 pattern indicating link up.
Vendor ID read returns valid value (expected 0x16C3ABCD per spec).
Command register accepts write of 0x7.
Memory base programming completes without error.
Cache coherency registers programmed and disabled correctly.
BAR size detection returns correct mask values.
BAR programming and readback match expected addresses.
Test completion flag 0x12345678 detected at 0xE6004100.",COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF,0x1E8,PF0_PORT_LOGIC,0x700,0x8E8,"CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_MODE, CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_MODE, CFG_MSTR_ARCACHE_VALUE, CFG_MSTR_AWCACHE_VALUE","[6:3], [14:11], [22:19], [30:27]","4, 4, 4, 4","rw, rw, rw, rw","0x0, 0x0, 0x0, 0x0",Read-Modify-Write,"0xF (cache mode/value enable), 0x0 (cache disable)",PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_device_enumerate_test/program.c,"mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF, mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF",Cache coherency programming for both PCIE0 and PCIE1 instances with enable and disable sequences
2,pcie_device_enumerate_test,PCIe Device Enumeration Test - BAR Register Access,Verify BAR0 register read/write for device enumeration,Functional,"Step 1: Write 0xFFFFFFFF to BAR registers at offsets 0x10 through 0x24 via pcie_slv0 and pcie_slv1.
Step 2: Read back BAR registers to determine BAR size.
Step 3: Program BAR registers with target addresses (0x0, 0x4, 0x20000000, 0x40000000, 0x60000000, 0x80000000).
Step 4: Read back programmed values to verify.","BAR size detection returns correct mask.
Programmed BAR values read back correctly.",BAR0_REG,0x10,PF0_TYPE1_HDR,0x0,0x10,"BAR0_MEM_IO, BAR0_TYPE, BAR0_PREFETCH, BAR0_START","[0], [2:1], [3], [31:4]","1, 2, 1, 28","ru, ru, ru, other","0x0, 0x2, 0x0, 0x0",Write then Read,"0xFFFFFFFF (size detect), then actual base addresses",PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_device_enumerate_test/program.c,write_pcie_slv0_reg / read_pcie_slv0_reg / write_pcie_slv1_reg / read_pcie_slv1_reg,BAR registers accessed via PCIe slave interface for both slv0 and slv1
3,pcie_device_enumerate_test,PCIe Device Enumeration Test - BAR1 Register Access,Verify BAR1 register read/write for device enumeration,Functional,"Step 1: Write 0xFFFFFFFF to BAR1 register at offset 0x14.
Step 2: Read back to determine BAR1 size.
Step 3: Program BAR1 with target address 0x4.
Step 4: Read back to verify.","BAR1 size detection returns correct mask.
Programmed value reads back as 0x4.",BAR1_REG,0x14,PF0_TYPE1_HDR,0x0,0x14,"BAR1_MEM_IO, BAR1_TYPE, BAR1_PREFETCH, BAR1_START","[0], [2:1], [3], [31:4]","1, 2, 1, 28","other, other, other, other","0x0, 0x0, 0x0, 0x0",Write then Read,"0xFFFFFFFF, 0x4",PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_device_enumerate_test/program.c,write_pcie_slv0_reg / read_pcie_slv0_reg,BAR1 accessed via PCIe slave interface
4,pcie_device_enumerate_test,PCIe Device Enumeration Test - Vendor ID Read,Verify Vendor ID is readable from PCIe configuration space,Functional,"Step 1: Read TYPE1_DEV_ID_VEND_ID_REG at offset 0x0 via pcie_slv0.
Step 2: Print and verify Vendor ID value.","Vendor ID read returns 0x16C3 (lower 16 bits).
Device ID returns 0xABCD (upper 16 bits).",TYPE1_DEV_ID_VEND_ID_REG,0x0,PF0_TYPE1_HDR,0x0,0x0,"VENDOR_ID, DEVICE_ID","[15:0], [31:16]","16, 16","ro, ro","0x16C3, 0xABCD",Read,N/A,PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_device_enumerate_test/program.c,read_pcie_slv0_reg(0x0),Read-only register for device identification
5,pcie_device_enumerate_test,PCIe Device Enumeration Test - Command Register Write,Verify Command Register write to enable IO/Memory/BusMaster,Functional,"Step 1: Write 0x7 to TYPE1_STATUS_COMMAND_REG at offset 0x4 via pcie_slv0.
Step 2: This sets IO_EN=1 MSE=1 BME=1.","Command register accepts write of 0x7.
IO Space Enable Memory Space Enable and Bus Master Enable bits are set.",TYPE1_STATUS_COMMAND_REG,0x4,PF0_TYPE1_HDR,0x0,0x4,"IO_EN, MSE, BME","[0], [1], [2]","1, 1, 1","other, other, rw","0x0, 0x0, 0x0",Write,0x7,PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_device_enumerate_test/program.c,write_pcie_slv0_reg(0x4 0x7),Enables IO Memory and Bus Master access
6,pcie_dma_write_test,PCIe DMA Write Test - DMA Write Interrupt Mask Configuration,Configure DMA write and read interrupt masks to enable all interrupts,Functional,"Step 1: Write 0x0 to DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF to unmask all DMA write interrupts (clear WR_DONE_INT_MASK and WR_ABORT_INT_MASK).
Step 2: Write 0x0 to DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF to unmask all DMA read interrupts (clear RD_DONE_INT_MASK and RD_ABORT_INT_MASK).","DMA write interrupt mask register set to 0x0 - all write done and abort interrupts unmasked.
DMA read interrupt mask register set to 0x0 - all read done and abort interrupts unmasked.",DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF,0x54,PF0_DMA_CAP,0x380000,0x380054,"WR_DONE_INT_MASK, WR_ABORT_INT_MASK","[3:0], [19:16]","4, 4","rw, rw","0xF, 0xF",Write,0x0 (unmask all interrupts),PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_dma_write_test/program.c,"mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF, mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF",Unmasks all 4 DMA write channel interrupts for both PCIE0 and PCIE1
7,pcie_dma_write_test,PCIe DMA Write Test - DMA Read Interrupt Mask Configuration,Configure DMA read interrupt masks to enable all interrupts,Functional,"Step 1: Write 0x0 to DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF to unmask all DMA read interrupts.","DMA read interrupt mask register set to 0x0 - all read done and abort interrupts unmasked.",DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF,0xA8,PF0_DMA_CAP,0x380000,0x3800A8,"RD_DONE_INT_MASK, RD_ABORT_INT_MASK","[3:0], [19:16]","4, 4","rw, rw","0xF, 0xF",Write,0x0 (unmask all interrupts),PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_dma_write_test/program.c,"mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF, mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF",Unmasks all 4 DMA read channel interrupts for both PCIE0 and PCIE1
8,pcie_dma_write_test,PCIe DMA Write Test - DMA Write Doorbell Trigger for Channels 0-3,Trigger DMA write transfers on all 4 channels by writing to DMA Write Doorbell register,Functional,"Step 1: Program DMA write channel 0 using program_dma_wch0 with source and destination addresses and length 0x40.
Step 2: Write 0x0 to DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF to trigger Channel 0 write transfer.
Step 3: Wait for interrupt (int_pend goes to 0).
Step 4: Program DMA write channel 1 and write 0x1 to DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF.
Step 5: Wait for interrupt.
Step 6: Program DMA write channel 2 and write 0x2 to DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF.
Step 7: Wait for interrupt.
Step 8: Program DMA write channel 3 and write 0x3 to DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF.
Step 9: Wait for interrupt.","Each DMA write channel transfer completes successfully.
Interrupt is generated for each channel completion.
DMA write doorbell register accepts channel numbers 0-3.",DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF,0x10,PF0_DMA_CAP,0x380000,0x380010,"WR_DOORBELL_NUM, WR_STOP","[2:0], [31]","3, 1","other, other","0x0, 0x0",Write,"0x0 (Ch0), 0x1 (Ch1), 0x2 (Ch2), 0x3 (Ch3)",PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_dma_write_test/program.c,"mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF, mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_DMA_WRITE_DOORBELL_OFF",Sequential DMA write transfers on channels 0-3 with interrupt-driven completion
9,pcie_dma_write_test,PCIe DMA Write Test - DMA Read Doorbell Trigger for Channels 0-3,Trigger DMA read transfers on all 4 channels by writing to DMA Read Doorbell register,Functional,"Step 1: Program DMA read channel 0 using program_dma_rch0 with source and destination addresses and length 0x40.
