27,pcie_reg_wr_rd_test,PCIe Register Write Read Test - PHY Register Reset Value and Read-Write Check,Verify PHY register reset values and read-write with PHY-specific patterns,Functional,"Step 1: Assert PHY reset by writing 0x01203000 to PCIE0_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL and PCIE1_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL.
Step 2: Read PHY registers at addresses 0xE68860B8 0xE68862B8 0xE68864B8 for PCIE0.
Step 3: Apply 16-bit extraction based on address alignment (lower 16 bits if even-aligned upper 16 bits if odd-aligned).
Step 4: Verify reset values are 0x0.
Step 5: Repeat for PCIE1 PHY registers at 0xE68A60B8 0xE68A62B8 0xE68A64B8.
Step 6: Write PHY test patterns (0x7BAF 0x1 0x003B) masked with 0x1FFF to PHY registers.
Step 7: Read back and verify (data & 0x1FFF) matches (pattern & 0x1FFF).","PHY registers read back reset value of 0x0 after PHY reset assertion.
PHY register write-read with 13-bit mask (0x1FFF) succeeds for all patterns.
PHY registers correctly handle 16-bit sub-register access.",PHY Registers (External),N/A,PHY (External to DBI),N/A,"0xE68860B8, 0xE68862B8, 0xE68864B8 (PCIE0); 0xE68A60B8, 0xE68A62B8, 0xE68A64B8 (PCIE1)",N/A,"[12:0] (write mask 0x1FFF)",13,rw,0x0,Write then Read,"0x7BAF & 0x1FFF, 0x1 & 0x1FFF, 0x003B & 0x1FFF",PCIE,TestRepo/PCIE/pcie_reg_wr_rd_test/program.c,"mizar_PCIE0_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL, mizar_PCIE1_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL",PHY registers accessed via direct memory-mapped addresses with 13-bit write mask